  <p class="lead"><strong>A Dairy Queen kids meal costs about $4.99 and comes with a kid-size entrée, fries or applesauce, milk or a soft drink, and a small vanilla cone.</strong> You choose a cheeseburger, 2 chicken strips or a hot dog. With fries and the cone, the meals run from about 650 to 750 calories. Below are the details for each meal, the lighter swaps, allergen pointers and how the kids meal compares with DQ’s value deals for older kids. Prices are typical and vary by location.</p>

  <h2 id="kids-meals-at-a-glance">DQ kids meals at a glance</h2>
  <p>All three kids meals cost the same, so the choice comes down to what your child will eat. Here is how they compare.</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="size-table">
