        <tr><td><strong><a href="/items/kids-hot-dog-meal">Kids Hot Dog Meal</a></strong></td><td>Hot dog on a bun</td><td class="price-cell">$4.99</td><td>~650</td><td>~440</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong><a href="/items/kids-cheeseburger-meal">Kids Cheeseburger Meal</a></strong></td><td>Kid-size cheeseburger</td><td class="price-cell">$4.99</td><td>~700</td><td>~490</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong><a href="/items/kids-chicken-strips-meal">Kids Chicken Strips Meal</a></strong></td><td>2 chicken strips with a dipping sauce</td><td class="price-cell">$4.99</td><td>~750</td><td>~540</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>The full menu, with the side and drink choices spelled out, is on our <a href="/categories/kids-meals">DQ kids meals page</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="whats-in-each-meal">What comes in each DQ kids meal</h2>
  <p>Every kids meal has the same four parts: an entrée, a side, a drink and a small vanilla cone. Only the entrée changes.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Entrée:</strong> a kid-size cheeseburger, 2 breaded chicken strips, or a hot dog.</li>
    <li><strong>Side:</strong> fries or applesauce.</li>
    <li><strong>Drink:</strong> milk or a soft drink.</li>
    <li><strong>Dessert:</strong> a small <a href="/items/vanilla-soft-serve-cone">vanilla soft serve cone</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Kids Hot Dog Meal</h3>
  <p>The hot dog meal is the lightest of the three at about 650 calories with fries and the cone. It is a good pick for smaller kids or anyone who eats slowly, since a hot dog is easy to hold and finish.</p>

  <h3>Kids Cheeseburger Meal</h3>
  <p>The cheeseburger is a smaller patty than the full-size Original Cheeseburger, so it suits a young appetite. The meal is about 700 calories with fries and the cone.</p>

  <h3>Kids Chicken Strips Meal</h3>
  <p>This is the most filling kids meal at about 750 calories with fries and the cone. It comes with one dipping sauce, such as ranch, honey mustard, BBQ or gravy. Most kids can finish two strips. For an extra-hungry child, add a side of fries or an order of <a href="/items/2pc-chicken-strips">2-piece chicken strips</a> (about $3.49).</p>

  <h2 id="is-it-good-value">Is the DQ kids meal a good deal?</h2>
  <p>Yes. The cone alone makes it one of the better-value kids meals in fast food. Take the hot dog meal as an example. Bought one by one, a hot dog costs about $3.99, a small fries about $2.49 and a small vanilla cone about $1.79. That is about $8.27 before you add a drink. The kids meal gets you all of it plus a drink for about $4.99, a saving of at least $3.28.</p>
  <p>The same logic applies to the strips meal. It costs only $1.50 more than 2-piece strips on their own, and that $1.50 covers the side, the drink and the cone.</p>

  <h2 id="lighter-swaps">How to make a DQ kids meal lighter</h2>
  <p>The easiest change is the side. Applesauce is about 50 calories, compared with about 260 for fries, so the swap takes about 210 calories off any kids meal.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Choose applesauce:</strong> the hot dog meal drops to about 440 calories, the cheeseburger meal to about 490 and the chicken strips meal to about 540, all with the cone still included.</li>
    <li><strong>Choose milk over soda:</strong> it is the better everyday drink for kids and skips the sugary fountain soda.</li>
    <li><strong>Save the cone for later:</strong> if you are eating in, you can ask the crew to hold the cone until your child finishes the meal, so it does not melt on the table.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>For calorie numbers across the rest of the menu, see our <a href="/blog/dairy-queen-calories-nutrition-guide">Dairy Queen calories guide</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="age-guidance">What age is the DQ kids meal for?</h2>
  <p>Kids meals are sized for younger children. Our kids meals page suggests roughly 12 and under as a guide, but DQ does not set a strict age limit at the register. In practice, most preschool and early grade-school kids are well served by one. Tweens and teens with bigger appetites often want more food, which is where the value deals come in (see below). Adults who want a small meal can order a kids meal too.</p>

  <h2 id="best-kid-treats">Best DQ treats for kids</h2>
  <p>If the included cone is not enough, or you are stopping just for dessert, the best kid-size picks are the small treats with a fixed portion. These are the ones parents tend to reach for.</p>
